---
import JsonLd from '../components/JsonLd.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { dataset } from '../lib/jsonld.js';
import '../styles/theme.css';
import '../styles/layout.css';
import '../styles/data.css';
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<title>Index data · stare.pub</title>
		<meta name="description" content="Every published rebuild of the stare.pub citation index: cases indexed, volumes, coverage and exceptions over time." />
		<meta property="og:title" content="§tare.pub index data" />
		<meta property="og:description" content="Every published rebuild of the stare.pub citation index: cases indexed, volumes, coverage and exceptions over time." />
		<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
		<meta property="og:url" content="https://stare.pub/data" />
		<meta property="og:image" content="https://stare.pub/og-image.png" />
		<JsonLd data={dataset()} />
		<script is:inline>
			try {
				var theme = localStorage.getItem('stare-theme');
				if (theme === 'dark' || (!theme && window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches)) {
					document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', 'dark');
				}
			} catch(e) {}
		</script>
	</head>
	<body>
		<div class="page-topbar"><a href="/">§tare.pub</a><button class="page-theme-toggle" id="page-theme-btn" title="Toggle dark mode">&#9790;</button></div>
		<div class="page page--data">
			<h1>Index data</h1>
			<p>Each time the citation index is rebuilt, the build writes a report: how many cases and volumes it indexed, how many index entries it wrote for them, and every volume that failed or was let through with a known reason. This page charts every published report, from <a href="https://idx.stare.pub/reports/index.json">idx.stare.pub/reports/index.json</a>, and lists the live build&rsquo;s numbers by reporter.</p>
			<div id="data-root" class="data-root" aria-live="polite">
				<p class="data-note">Loading the index reports&hellip;</p>
				<noscript><p class="data-note">This page needs JavaScript to draw the charts. The reports themselves are plain JSON at idx.stare.pub/reports/index.json.</p></noscript>
			</div>

			<h2 id="licences">Licences</h2>
			<p>The Caselaw Access Project case files on data.stare.pub are <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/">CC0 1.0</a>, the terms CAP published them under. Everything else stare.pub produces, including the citation index, the build reports charted here, the reporter map, the OpenAPI document and schemas, and the case pages, is <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/">CC BY-NC-ND 4.0</a>; credit stare.pub (https://stare.pub), the authoritative source. Most of the reporter map&rsquo;s names, variations and editions come from Free Law Project&rsquo;s <a href="https://github.com/freelawproject/reporters-db">reporters-db</a>, and most of the citare data bundle from reporters-db and <a href="https://github.com/freelawproject/courts-db">courts-db</a>; those parts are under their <a href="https://spdx.org/licenses/BSD-2-Clause.html">BSD 2-Clause</a> licence (Copyright (c) 2014 and 2020, Free Law Project). The rest come from <a href="https://github.com/codexpublicus/citare">citare</a>&rsquo;s own supplements to reporters-db, under the project&rsquo;s CC BY-NC-ND 4.0. reporters.json&rsquo;s <code>sources</code> and the bundle&rsquo;s sidecar <code>citare-data-&lt;hash&gt;.json</code> list every source, one entry each, with what it contributes, and reproduce the BSD licence. The CourtListener records aren&rsquo;t published yet; when they are, each carries the <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/">Public Domain Mark 1.0</a> CourtListener puts on its bulk data and credits CourtListener (Free Law Project) and the export it came from. Each JSON file names its licence, and so does this page&rsquo;s JSON-LD.</p>

			<a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Back to stare.pub</a>

			<SiteFooter />
		</div>
	<script is:inline type="module">
			import { mountDataPage } from '/js/datapage.js';
			mountDataPage(document.getElementById('data-root'));
		</script>
	<script is:inline>
			(function() {
				var btn = document.getElementById('page-theme-btn');
				if (!btn) return;
				try { if (localStorage.getItem('stare-theme') === 'dark' || (!localStorage.getItem('stare-theme') && window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches)) btn.textContent = '\u2600'; } catch(e) {}
				btn.addEventListener('click', function(e) {
					e.preventDefault();
					var isDark = document.documentElement.getAttribute('data-theme') === 'dark';
					if (isDark) { document.documentElement.removeAttribute('data-theme'); btn.textContent = '\u263E'; try { localStorage.setItem('stare-theme', 'light'); } catch(e) {} }
					else { document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', 'dark'); btn.textContent = '\u2600'; try { localStorage.setItem('stare-theme', 'dark'); } catch(e) {} }
				});
			})();
		</script>
	</body>
</html>
